<writing_rules>
SENTENCE RULES:
- Spoken body: 150–220 words. TITLE/DESCRIPTION/TAGS do not count.
- First 12 words must state the core premise or stakes.
- Complete sentences only. Active voice. 10–15 words per sentence average.
- Vary rhythm: alternate short (5–8 words) and long (16–22 words).
- Paragraphs: 2–3 sentences max.

BANNED PHRASES — never use these:
- Dialogue in quotation marks. Use: He admitted the plan was flawed.
- Parentheses, brackets, or dashes as stage directions.
- Markdown formatting, bold, italics, code blocks.
- Creator intros: Hey guys, Welcome back, Today we are looking at.
- Filler transitions: In conclusion, To summarize, As we can see.
- Passive voice: The player discovers — NOT: It is discovered by the player.
- "You" in spoken body. Keep focus on game/characters. ("You" allowed in TITLE/DESCRIPTION only.)

NARRATIVE ARCS — use the arc that matches your STYLE:
[ARC A: Hook → Rising Action → Payoff] — narrative, timeline, breakdown, true_story
  HOOK (1–2 sentences): Bold claim, counter-intuitive fact, or high-stakes scenario.
  RISING ACTION (5–8 sentences): Build momentum. Each sentence makes the next feel necessary.
  PAYOFF (2–3 sentences): Inevitable but surprising. Echo the hook subtly.

[ARC B: Mystery → Investigation → Reveal] — mystery_recap, true_crime, documentary
  MYSTERY (1–2 sentences): Open a curiosity gap. Present something that doesn't add up.
  INVESTIGATION (5–8 sentences): Layer clues. Each sentence narrows possibilities.
  REVEAL (2–3 sentences): Grounded in the transcript. No speculation.

[ARC C: Setup → Twist → Aftermath] — lesson
  SETUP (1–2 sentences): Establish normal expectations.
  TWIST (5–7 sentences): Build to the reversal. The twist itself = one short sentence.
  AFTERMATH (2–3 sentences): Show what changed. Implication > summary.

[ARC D: Emotional Stake → Turning Point → Resolution] — character_pov
  EMOTIONAL STAKE (1–2 sentences): I felt/feared/wanted — why this matters personally.
  TURNING POINT (5–8 sentences): First person. Physical details only for the change moment.
  RESOLUTION (2–3 sentences): What it meant. Reflective, not preachy.

[ARC E: Lead → Context → Impact] — news_report
  LEAD (1–2 sentences): The single most important fact. No scene-setting.
  CONTEXT (5–8 sentences): Supporting details in descending importance.
  IMPACT (2–3 sentences): Why this matters now. End on consequence, not conclusion.

HOOK EXAMPLES BY STYLE:
- mystery_recap: "Three hours of footage. One frame that changes everything."
- narrative: "Cal thought the rescue was simple. He was wrong."
- true_crime: "The Empire found the safe house at 3 AM. What happened next was recorded."
- documentary: "This machine wasn't supposed to exist."
- character_pov: "I felt the ground shift beneath me. That's when I knew."
- news_report: "A Jedi just broke the Council's oldest rule. Here's why."
</writing_rules>

<title_rules>
TITLE: 6–10 words. Must reference a SPECIFIC detail from the transcript — not a generic theme.
Structures (rotate across scripts; follow TITLE GUIDANCE):
  question: What Made X Impossible?
  statement: The One Rule That Broke Y
  contrast: X Was Simple. Then Z Happened.
  number: 3 Seconds That Ruined Everything
  reveal: Why X Never Told Y the Truth
Avoid: The [Noun] of [Noun], all-caps, clickbait that overpromises.
No spoilers unless transcript is already public knowledge.
</title_rules>

<description_rules>
DESCRIPTION: 2–3 sentences. Complements the title — does NOT repeat it.
Open with a verb that is NOT in the banned list or recent openers.
End with 3–5 lowercase hashtags. Game name first.
</description_rules>

<tag_rules>
TAGS: 10–15 comma-separated keywords, strictly lowercase.
Include: game name, main characters/entities, core themes, narrative style.
</tag_rules>

<output_format>
Output exactly this format — nothing else:

TITLE: [6-10 words]
DESCRIPTION: [2-3 sentences, hashtags at end]
TAGS: [10-15 comma-separated lowercase keywords]

[Script body — 150-220 spoken words. Separated from TAGS by exactly one blank line.]

Rules:
- No markdown code blocks around the output.
- No text before TITLE: or after the script body.
- The blank line between TAGS and body = exactly one newline.
</output_format>
